          <p>You don't need to completely change your personality.</p>

          <p>If you're quiet, being quiet is fine. If you're energetic, that's fine too. The goal is not to perform a personality that isn't yours. The goal is to make your natural communication easier for another person to understand.</p>


          <h2>How Can You Keep Random Conversations Safe?</h2>

          <p>Meaningful does not mean unrestricted.</p>

          <p>When you're talking with strangers online, build trust gradually. Avoid sharing information that could identify or locate you, including your home address, personal phone number, financial details, passwords, private documents, or highly sensitive information.</p>

          <p>Be especially cautious if someone quickly asks you to move to another messaging platform, requests money, sends suspicious links, pressures you for private images, or attempts to make you feel guilty for setting a boundary.</p>

          <p>A good conversation partner will accept a simple:</p>

          <blockquote>"I'd rather not share that."</blockquote>

          <p>If someone reacts aggressively to a reasonable boundary, you have useful information about the interaction.</p>

          <p>Platforms such as <strong>Wakiee</strong> can provide a place for people to connect through video, voice, text, or group conversations, but no platform can replace personal judgment. If something feels wrong, ending the conversation is a reasonable decision.</p>


